      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of rotting is a heavy weight, but it's also a sign that you've reached a point where the old ways of doing things are no longer serving you. If the pressure of trying to recapture a past glory is suffocating you, maybe the most immediate relief is to stop trying to produce anything at all. Give yourself permission to step away from the gear and the expectations, because sometimes the only way to truly feel like you're moving forward is to simply stop moving in the direction you've been forced to go.",
